@@ -0,0 +1,119 @@
+# v2 pace tuning — MM-calibrated packet pace + terminal spawn cadence
+
+Two feel fixes from the user's 2026-08-21 live play session (briefing
+`packet-plumber-v2-pace-tuning`, both rulings already in direction):
+
+1. **Packet pace → Mini Motorways car pace.** `packet_bandwidth` (balance.json)
+   is THE single named pace knob: **30 → 120 (4×)** — the top of the ruling's
+   2.5–4× ballpark. Transit ticks = ceil(packet_bandwidth / pipe capacity)
+   scale linearly; the 5.9 spawn-credit accrual divides by it, so the demand
+   stays **units-anchored** — the time axis stretches, the network's workload
+   (units/s) is unchanged.
+2. **Terminal spawn cadence ↓.** The growth cadence consts migrated to
+   balance.json (the 5.6 placement-block precedent — this job's legitimate
+   re-bless): `terminal_spawn_interval_ticks` **40 → 80** (one terminal per
+   4 s, was 2 s — the 2× reduction) and `terminal_min_sep_tiles` **3 → 4**
+   (the added cluster spacing). Both named knobs the user iterates on.
+
+## Before / after numbers (measured, same seeds)
+
+**Transit — per edge, email class (the catalog arithmetic, verified by the
+harness stats stream):**
+
+| path | before | after | scale |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| standard pipe (cap 15) | 2 ticks = 100 ms | 8 ticks = 400 ms | 4× |
+| wide fiber (cap 40) | 1 tick = 50 ms | 3 ticks = 150 ms | 3× |
+| narrow (cap 10) | 3 ticks = 150 ms | 12 ticks = 600 ms | 4× |
+| board crossing (4–6 standard edges) | ~0.4–0.6 s | **~1.6–2.4 s** | >1.5 s floor ✓ |
+| typical route, estate_surge demo (measured `--stats-out`): email | 172 ms | **555 ms** | 3.2× |
+| typical route, estate_surge demo: streaming | 252 ms | **412 ms** | 1.6× |
+| congested surge demo: streaming avg | 1 569 ms | **5 794 ms** | 3.7× |
+
+The per-edge ratio is exactly 4× for the integer ceil math; the measured
+route averages land 1.6–3.7× (the route mix of wide/standard edges +
+queueing phases). The board-crossing floor (>1.5 s) is met on the standard
+backbone; the wide-fiber express path stays the fastest (its throughput is
+the point) — if the fun-test still reads fast there, `packet_bandwidth` is a
+one-line knob (150/180/240).
+
+**Terminal spawns:**
+
+| knob | before | after |
+|---|---|---|
+| spawn interval | 40 ticks = 1 per 2 s (~30/min) | **80 ticks = 1 per 4 s (~15/min)** |
+| min separation | 3 tiles | **4 tiles** |
+
+## Time-axis coherence (why the tolerances scaled with the knob)
+
+`latency_tol_ms` (email 500→2000, streaming 300→1200) and the E30 exit
+margin (40→160) scale 4× **with** the pace: they are wall-time deadlines
+vs 4× longer transits — leaving them would make the game 4× harder, a
+gameplay-semantics change the ruling forbids. The breach semantics are
+preserved (measured: the estate_surge email avg 555 ms vs the 2000 ms
+tolerance — same 3.2× headroom as before). Wall-anchored tick values
+(health window, warning leads, era-advance window, grace) are untouched.
+
+**Known consequences, documented honestly:**
+- The ×10 surge's *packet* multiplicativity dims at the 4× pace (measured
+  ~2.6× in units): the packet-denominated ask (20/tick) can't express above
+  the units-anchored credit pool. The fair-crisis saturation trigger still
+  fires and the aggregation event still lands at the estate uplink (W9
+  re-derived to the units-anchored floor — the base ask alone would source
+  only 2/tick, the pin bites). Watch in the fun-test.
+- The per-terminal burst ceilings (host 2 / campus 3 at 30 u) degenerate to
+  `max(1, ceil(cap)) = 1` uniformly at the 4× pace (the MAX_CREDIT clamp);
+  the burst-latency guard holds via the 4×-scaled tolerances.
+- The credit clamp also makes the per-terminal pick rate
+  `1 / ceil(1000/accrue)` per tick (campus 0.5/tick, host 0.25/tick) — the
+  demand tests re-derive from that exact bound (measured, never guessed).
+
+## Golden re-bless (deliberate, cause-documented)
+
+All 45 demos' T1 manifests + action logs + T2 captures and the input-parity
+manifests re-blessed (`harness save` + `harness input-parity save`, harness
+rebuilt from the new core first). Every shift is caused by (a) the
+catalog_hash fold (the new knob values + comments) and (b) the genuine
+behavioral change (packet positions, spawn times — the point of the story).
+Replay gate: every blessed log re-sims its manifest bit-for-bit; the local
+CI suite is **10/10 green** (`tools/ci-local.sh --mac`).
+
+## Tests
+
+46 pace-related pins re-pinned across 17 test files (exact-tick/unit pins
+re-derived from measured runs — never guessed), two stagings re-staged (the
+crisis (b)-drop-fallback regime: deterministic 4-5/tick seed arrivals so the
+post-shed eval lane sits below the bound at the trigger tick; the health
+grace/meter tests: the post-fix exit offset + expiry re-measured and the fix
+re-staged at 300), and the demand contracts (W9/W10/director counts,
+terminal-class profiles, credit accrue/ceil table) re-derived to the
+units-anchored + clamp-honest forms.
+
+## Decisions & rationale
+
+- **`packet_bandwidth` IS the pace knob** — the briefing's "single pace-scale
+  knob", already named and catalog-resident; transit scales linearly and the
+  demand is units-anchored by construction (no new indirection field, no
+  second number to drift).
+- **SLA tolerances + exit margin scale with the knob** — required for "no
+  gameplay-semantics change" (see above); scoped to the time axis only.
+- **Demand volumes untouched** — the credit gate already makes them
+  units-anchored; touching them would be a semantic change.
+- **Growth consts → balance.json** — the 5.6 placement-block precedent at a
+  legitimate re-bless; the knobs are the iteration surface the user asked
+  for. `radius_tiles` (5) still exceeds the new floor (4); the loader
+  validation updated to the catalog field.
+- **Skill waiver carried as a canon note**: the briefing's `bmad-quick-dev`
+  forwards to bmad-build, which fails on this install (`ambiguous config
+  token implementation_artifacts` — Silas ruling 2026-08-21, field notes);
+  executed self-contained from the briefing instead.
+- **Out of scope (per the briefing):** routing semantics, serialization,
+  packet contracts, LOG_VERSION — all untouched. Visual/aesthetic surface
+  untouched (the design-audit job owns it; this branch stays unmerged until
+  its Perkins verdict, per the dispatch note).
+
+## Fun-test gate
+
+Merge ≠ done: the user plays `odin run app` after merge; the knobs
+(`packet_bandwidth`, `terminal_spawn_interval_ticks`, `terminal_min_sep_tiles`)
+are the expected iteration surface for the follow-up tuning round.
